{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useHeldKeyCodes(): Record<string, string>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/react-hotkeys/src/useHeldKeyCodes.ts#L30","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useHeldKeyCodes.ts:30"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React hook that returns a map of currently held key names to their physical "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"event.code"},{"type":"text","value":" values."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is useful for debugging which physical key was pressed (e.g. distinguishing\nleft vs right Shift via \"ShiftLeft\" / \"ShiftRight\")."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Record mapping normalized key names to their "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"event.code"},{"type":"text","value":" values"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function KeyDebugDisplay() {\n  const heldKeys = useHeldKeys()\n  const heldCodes = useHeldKeyCodes()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {heldKeys.map((key) => (\n        <kbd key={key}>\n          {key} <small>{heldCodes[key]}</small>\n        </kbd>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useHeldKeyCodes(): Record<string, string>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHeldKeyCodes.ts:30](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/react-hotkeys/src/useHeldKeyCodes.ts#L30)\n\nReact hook that returns a map of currently held key names to their physical `event.code` values.\n\nThis is useful for debugging which physical key was pressed (e.g. distinguishing\nleft vs right Shift via \"ShiftLeft\" / \"ShiftRight\").\n\n## Returns\n\n`Record`\\<`string`, `string`\\>\n\nRecord mapping normalized key names to their `event.code` values\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nfunction KeyDebugDisplay() {\n  const heldKeys = useHeldKeys()\n  const heldCodes = useHeldKeyCodes()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {heldKeys.map((key) => (\n        <kbd key={key}>\n          {key} <small>{heldCodes[key]}</small>\n        </kbd>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useHeldKeyCodes\ntitle: useHeldKeyCodes\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useHeldKeyCodes(): Record<string, string>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHeldKeyCodes.ts:30](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/react-hotkeys/src/useHeldKeyCodes.ts#L30)\n\nReact hook that returns a map of currently held key names to their physical `event.code` values.\n\nThis is useful for debugging which physical key was pressed (e.g. distinguishing\nleft vs right Shift via \"ShiftLeft\" / \"ShiftRight\").\n\n## Returns\n\n`Record`\\<`string`, `string`\\>\n\nRecord mapping normalized key names to their `event.code` values\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nfunction KeyDebugDisplay() {\n  const heldKeys = useHeldKeys()\n  const heldCodes = useHeldKeyCodes()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {heldKeys.map((key) => (\n        <kbd key={key}>\n          {key} <small>{heldCodes[key]}</small>\n        </kbd>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n"}
